  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 202 AM CDT Wed Jul 22 2026\n\nHigh pressure and northwest flow will keep us cool and dry. With\nthe center of the high moving over us today we will also see\nlight winds. This pattern will continue through the end of the\nweek. Once we get into the weekend the pattern will shift as a\nridge builds into the central CONUS. This will bring increased\nheat and humidity. Temperatures back into the 90s look likely \nfor the weekend. Warmer than normal temperatures look to\ncontinue into next week, but less likely to see 90s. Unlike out\nlast round of heat we are not expecting to see the center of the\nupper high over us. It will be to our south with the ridge\noverhead, which will allow for shortwaves to move along this\nbroader flow. Still seeing a very scattered solution within the\nensemble members with little increase in clustering compared to\na day ago. For the first chance on Saturday there is some\nclustering around a likely solution, but that remains up north\ncloser to the international border. Sunday into Monday's chances\nremain more widely scattered. In summary little in the forecast\nhas changed over the past day. The thesis of the forecast is\nstill seasonably cool and dry becomes hot and humid this \nweekend with uncertain rain/storm chances.",
